From e3e3500fe4946d5e0b1027da12d23ac37a411532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qasim Ijaz <Qasim.Ijaz@analog.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:30:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: Add delay before initial root port reset

The ADSP-SC589-MINI and ADSP-SC573 can fail to detect certain older
or slower USB devices in U-Boot. Running "usb start" may fail while
the USB device is plugged in:

=> usb start
starting USB...
USB device descriptor short read (expected 8, got 0)
Scanning bus musb@310c1000 failed, error -5
Bus musb@310c1000: No USB Device found
       scanning usb for storage devices... 0 Storage Device(s) found

The same device is detected and operates correctly after booting Linux.

Add a 500 ms delay in musb_lowlevel_init() before the initial root
port reset. This gives the USB device additional settling time before
U-Boot begins the root port reset via _musb_reset_root_port().

Signed-off-by: Qasim Ijaz <Qasim.Ijaz@analog.com>
---
 drivers/usb/musb-new/musb_uboot.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb-new/musb_uboot.c b/drivers/usb/musb-new/musb_uboot.c
index 43ab3245e5c..4c27c993189 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb-new/musb_uboot.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb-new/musb_uboot.c
@@ -239,6 +239,8 @@ int musb_lowlevel_init(struct musb_host_data *host)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
+	mdelay(500);
+
 	_musb_reset_root_port(host, NULL);
 	host->host->is_active = 1;
 	host->hcd.hcd_priv = host->host;
-- 
2.43.0

